    Developer and including the name of the Initial Developer in (a) the
    Source Code, and (b) in any notice in an Executable then in
    existence, and (c) in a patent infringement claim or notice
    regarding the Modification.

3.4. Intellectual Property Matters.
    (a) Third Party Claims.
        If You have knowledge that a party or parties are making a claim
        of patent infringement (or threats of such claims) regarding a
        Modification made by You, You may choose, with respect to such
        Modification only, to (i) negotiate with the claimant with
        respect to such claim, (ii) if such claim is not withdrawn,
        remove such Modification from Your Covered Code distribution, or
        (iii) if such claim is withdrawn, include such Modification in
        Your distribution.
    (b) Initiator of a Claim.
        If You initiate any litigation by asserting a patent
        infringement claim (excluding declaratory judgment actions)
        against Initial Developer or a Contributor (the Initial
        Developer or Contributor against whom You file the action) with
        respect to a Contributor Version (other than a Contributor
        Version you are using in combination with Your Modifications),
        then and only in that event, all rights, covenants and licenses
        granted by such Initial Developer or Contributor under Section 2
        shall immediately terminate unless the total patent claims
        asserted by You against all parties named in the lawsuit are
        withdrawn or settled.
    (c) If you assert a patent infringement claim against Initial
        Developer or a Contributor alleging that the Contributor Version
        directly or indirectly infringes any patent, all rights granted
        by such Initial Developer or Contributor to You under Sections
        2.1 and/or 2.2 of this License shall, upon 60 days notice from
        Initial Developer or Contributor (the "Notice Period") terminate
        prospectively, unless (1) within 60 days of the Notice Period,
        such Contributor withdraws its patent claim, or (2) You enter
        into a license agreement with the aggrieved Contributor within
        the Notice Period, or (3) You provide the aggrieved Contributor
        with a license to the patent claims asserted against such
        Contributor. If the Initial Developer or Contributor fails to
        timely notify You of the termination, You shall be entitled to
        continue using the Covered Code. If You fail to timely cure the
        breach as described in this Section 3.4(c), all of Your rights
        under this License shall terminate immediately.

