8. TERMINATION
--------------

8.1. This License and the rights granted hereunder will terminate
    automatically if You fail to comply with terms herein and fail to
    cure such breach within 30 days of becoming aware of the breach.
    All sublicenses to the Covered Code which are automatically granted
    by the Sections 2.2, 2.3, and 2.4 shall survive the termination of
    this License.

8.2. If You initiate litigation by asserting a patent infringement
    claim (excluding declaratory judgment actions) against Initial
    Developer or a Contributor with respect to a Contributor Version,
    then any and all rights granted by such Initial Developer or
    Contributor under Sections 2.1 and/or 2.2 of this License shall, upon
    60 days notice from Initial Developer or Contributor terminate
    prospectively, unless if within 60 days of receipt of notice (a) a
    settlement is reached with respect to the patent infringement claim
    against Initial Developer or Contributor, or (b) a court of competent
    jurisdiction determines that the patent infringement claim is
    unjustified. If the Initial Developer or Contributor fails to timely
    notify You of the termination, You shall be entitled to continue
    using the Covered Code. If You fail to timely cure the breach, then
    all of Your rights under this License shall terminate immediately.

8.3. If You assert a patent infringement claim against Participant
    alleging that the Contributor Version directly or indirectly
    infringes any patent where such claim is resolved (such as by
    license or settlement) prior to the initiation of patent infringement
    litigation, then the reasonable value of the licenses granted by such
    Contributor under Sections 2.1 or 2.2 shall be taken into account in
    determining the amount or value of any payment or license.

8.4. In the event of termination under Sections 8.1 or 8.2 above, all
    end user license agreements (excluding distributors and resellers)
    which have been validly granted by You or any distributor hereunder
    prior to termination shall survive termination.

